# KythOS updater signing keys — PLACEHOLDER, NO KEY MATERIAL.
#
# This file is the trust anchor for the signed updater manifest
# (docs/updater-signing.md). The rclone and GE-Proton runtime updaters
# verify the KythOS-signed update manifest against the OpenPGP primary
# key certificate(s) recorded here before installing anything.
#
# NO PRODUCTION KEY HAS BEEN INSTALLED YET. While this file contains
# no certificate, the updaters fail closed: every gated update is
# refused with a "signing key not installed yet" error and the current
# version keeps running. That is deliberate — the mechanism ships
# complete, the key does not exist yet.
#
# To install the real key: generate it OFFLINE on the key owner's own
# hardware (never on a build machine, never in CI, never by an
# automated tool), export ONLY the public certificate, and replace the
# contents of this file (build_files/config/updater-signing-keys.asc)
# with the armored public key block:
#
#   gpg --armor --export <key-id> > build_files/config/updater-signing-keys.asc
#
# The file is installed to /usr/share/kyth/updater-signing-keys.asc by
# build_files/scripts/branding/99-updater-signing-key.sh and reaches
# installed systems with the next image update. During a primary-key
# rotation this file may hold two certificates (old + new) so both
# verify during the overlap window.
